Mayflower is a technology company building large-scale entertainment products for a global audience. Our platforms serve millions of users worldwide and rank among the top-50 most visited websites globally. For more than 10 years, we've been creating reliable, high-performance solutions at the intersection of product, engineering, and entertainment.
We’re looking for a Brand Designer to craft visual assets for campaigns, social media, and events. Your role will be turning creative ideas into compelling static and animated designs.
Responsibilities:

• Create high-quality, brand-aligned visual assets across Brand Marketing touchpoints, including campaigns, social, product marketing, events, and merchandise;

• Bring motion into design work where appropriate, using animation and dynamic elements to enhance campaigns and content;

• Take ownership of motion work when relevant, helping bring ideas to life in a more engaging and impactful way;

• Translate creative briefs into strong visual concepts and execute them to a high standard across both static and motion outputs;

• Work closely with the Brand Design Supervisor and wider team to deliver consistent, on-brand creative across all outputs;

• Contribute to campaign development, supporting with visual ideas and ensuring strong integration between design and concept;

• Ensure all work aligns with brand guidelines, maintaining a high level of craft, consistency, and attention to detail;

• Prepare and deliver assets across multiple formats, including digital, print, and event environments;

• Collaborate with Brand Marketing, Social, Events, and Content teams to deliver creative that meets both brand and business needs.

Requirements
You’ll thrive here if you have

• 3+ years of experience in brand, marketing, or visual design roles;

• Portfolio showcasing high-quality, brand-aligned design work across a range of formats, including motion work;

• Experience working on brand campaigns within entertainment, creator-led, or culturally driven platforms;

• Solid design fundamentals, including typography, layout, composition, and visual hierarchy;

• Experience working across a range of formats, including digital, social, campaigns, and print;

• Experience with motion design tools (e.g. After Effects), with the ability to create simple animations and motion-based assets;

• Close attention to detail, with a strong sense of craft and consistency;

• Ability to translate creative direction into polished, high-quality outputs;

• Experience working on brand campaigns within entertainment, creator-led, or culturally driven platforms;

• Experience designing for live events, activations, or branded merchandise;

• Collaborative and comfortable working within a team structure under creative direction;

• Remote (EU time zone);

• Advanced English (written and spoken).

• Relevant degree or equivalent experience in design, visual communication, or a related field is a plus.

Conditions
We know that great talent deserves great conditions, so here's what you can expect when joining us:

• Full remote work.

• Competitive compensation with a service contract.

• Transparent performance reviews twice a year, with bonus opportunities and salary adjustments.

• An annual allowance that you can use for home office improvements, sports activities, equipment upgrades, and more-tailor it to what benefits you most.

• Investment in your development: paid language courses, access to various learning platforms, and a mindfulness benefit, including psychological support with 50% coverage.

• Career growth in a fast-scaling project with opportunities to influence technical decisions.

• A culture of recognition: our peer reward program celebrates contributions from across the team.

Benefits are provided in accordance with the company’s policies and eligibility criteria.
Recruitment process

• HR interview (40 min);

• Technical interview (1 hour);

• Test task;

• Final interview (1 hour);

